  "response_text": "It's important to be aware of any unusual symptoms, especially when it comes to discharge and irritation. Here are some signs you might watch for, expressed in a non-judgmental way:\n\n- If you notice any changes in the color, smell, or amount of discharge, this could be a sign that something isn't right.\n- If you experience itching, burning, or pain around the area, these could be signs of irritation or infection.\n- If you feel discomfort or a general sense of not feeling well, it might be worth paying attention to these symptoms.\n- If the irritation or discharge persists or gets worse, it's important to seek advice from a healthcare provider.\n\nRemember, these are just general signs and symptoms, and what might be normal for one person could be concerning for another. If you're unsure or if you have any concerns, it's always best to consult with a healthcare professional.",
